  {
    "episode_id": 95481,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95481.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, I respectfully disagree with the premise of the question. I would submit to you that the divide on crypto is not so much ideological or partisan, but it's generational. And the opposition to crypto is largely a gerontocracy. Yesterday, the financial services committee in the house passed a market structure bill on a bipartisan basis. And the bipartisan support came from younger Democrats like myself. who are open to embracing the potentialities of blockchain technology. So I see it as more as a generational divide. And as Congress becomes less of a jerry talkers to over time, I suspect the institution will become more open to embracing crypto.",
